  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "Mary’s top book shelf holds five books with the following widths, in centimeters: \\(6,\\) \\(\\dfrac{1}{2},\\) \\(1,\\) \\(2.5,\\) and \\(10.\\)\n\nWhat is the average book width, in centimeters?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(2\\)",
    "C": "\\(3\\)",
    "D": "\\(4\\)",
    "E": "\\(5\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The average width is the total width divided by the number of books. Using \\(\\frac12=0.5\\), the total is\n\\[\n6+0.5+1+2.5+10=20\n\\]\ncentimeters. There are five books, so the average is \\(20\\div5=\\boxed{4}\\) centimeters, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
